        "thinking": "Both `listInstalled` and `listByStatus` are pure DB queries — they just query the `plugins` table. No FS, no Node.js subprocess, no runtime state involved.\n\nSo `GET /api/plugins` CAN work in CF — it just queries the `plugins` table in the DB. The current `[]` stub is incorrect; it should return the actual plugins from the DB.\n\nHowever, the important question is: are plugins useful in the CF deployment? The plugins can be listed (DB-backed), but:\n- Plugin installation/uninstallation requires FS (installing npm packages to disk)\n\n\n- Plugin execution requires spawning child processes\n- Plugin UI contributions need the plugin to be loaded and running\n\nBut listing and fetching UI contributions are both DB-backed operations — the manifest is stored in the database, so `GET /api/plugins` and `GET /api/plugins/ui-contributions` can both work in CF by reading directly from the DB.\n\nNow I need to update the routes to actually query the plugins table instead of returning empty stubs. I'll implement `GET /api/plugins` to call `pluginRegistryService(db).listInstalled()` and `GET /api/plugins/ui-contributions` to extract UI contributions from the stored manifests of ready plugins. Let me check if the plugins table is properly imported.",
